    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get JWT Token (Cognito)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Extract and save JWT tokens from Cognito response",
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has authentication result', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('AuthenticationResult');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.AuthenticationResult).to.have.property('IdToken');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.AuthenticationResult).to.have.property('AccessToken');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.AuthenticationResult).to.have.property('RefreshToken');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Save the IdToken to collection variable for API requests",
                  "const response = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (response.AuthenticationResult && response.AuthenticationResult.IdToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('jwtToken', response.AuthenticationResult.IdToken);",
                  "    console.log('JWT Token saved to collection variable');",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Optionally save other tokens",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', response.AuthenticationResult.AccessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', response.AuthenticationResult.RefreshToken);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Amz-Target",
                "value": "AWSCognitoIdentityProviderService.InitiateAuth",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-amz-json-1.1",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"AuthFlow\": \"USER_PASSWORD_AUTH\",\n  \"ClientId\": \"{{userPoolClientId}}\",\n  \"AuthParameters\": {\n    \"USERNAME\": \"{{cognitoUsername}}\",\n    \"PASSWORD\": \"{{cognitoPassword}}\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://cognito-idp.{{awsRegion}}.amazonaws.com/",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": ["cognito-idp", "{{awsRegion}}", "amazonaws", "com"],
              "path": [""]
            },
            "description": "Authenticate with AWS Cognito using username and password to obtain JWT tokens.\n\n**Authentication Flow:** USER_PASSWORD_AUTH\n\n**Required Collection Variables:**\n- `userPoolClientId` - Cognito User Pool Client ID\n- `cognitoUsername` - User's email address\n- `cognitoPassword` - User's password\n- `awsRegion` - AWS region (default: eu-west-2)\n\n**Response Tokens:**\n- `IdToken` - Used for API authentication (saved to `jwtToken` variable)\n- `AccessToken` - Used for Cognito user operations\n- `RefreshToken` - Used to obtain new tokens\n\n**Token Expiry:**\n- Access Token: 60 minutes\n- ID Token: 60 minutes\n- Refresh Token: 30 days\n\n**Usage:**\n1. Set the required collection variables (userPoolClientId, cognitoUsername, cognitoPassword)\n2. Send this request\n3. The `jwtToken` variable will be automatically populated\n4. Use the token for protected API endpoints\n\n**Testing Custom Claims:**\nAfter authentication, you can decode the JWT at https://jwt.io to verify custom claims:\n- `custom:tenantId` - Tenant identifier\n- `custom:role` - User role (e.g., system_admin)\n- `custom:customerId` - Customer identifier (optional)"
          },
